omments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:e29b476d71d6bd2774aa4be809fe278b8a5681f2295b3121e211edc8ee46c36d","file":"preprints/Finite-cylinder-approximation-of-ruled-sets-September-27-2026/build/sections/product-methods.tex","line":12,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"db18863a5d99196df90ed627df1740f14408b6e6ad7c43a48dfef2a14817c2bf","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Finite-cylinder-approximation-of-ruled-sets-September-27-2026/build/sections/product-methods.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:e29b476d71d6bd2774aa4be809fe278b8a5681f2295b3121e211edc8ee46c36d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Finite-cylinder-approximation-of-ruled-sets-September-27-2026/build/sections/product-methods.tex#L12"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{b:product}\nLet $h,M>0$, let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^2$ be compact with\n$|\\partial D|=0$, and let $V$ be $C^1$ on an open neighborhood of $D$.\nSuppose that $DV(p)$ has eigenvalues $\\lambda_p,-\\lambda_p$, where\n$0<M\\lambda_p<1$ for every $p\\in D$.  For every $e>0$, the set\n\\[\n \\mathcal S_h(D,V,M)=\n \\{(x,p_1+xV_1(p),h(p_2+xV_2(p))):p\\in D,\\ |x|\\le M\\}\n\\]\nhas a finite cylinder cover with bounded open measurable perpendicular\nbases whose total area is at most\n\\[\n h\\int_D J_h(V(p))\\,dp+e,\n \\qquad J_h(w)=(1+w_1^2+h^2w_2^2)^{-1/2}.\n\\]"}
